Sval: Settings' form fields are neither saved with a tab nor put back

The session store saves the fields of a page with its tab and, when the
tab is restored, sets each one back and fires `input` on it
(SessionStoreUtils::RestoreFormData). Sval's switches and fields in
about:preferences write their prefs on `input`, so a Settings tab
restored at launch set every pref back to what its fields held when the
tab was last saved, undoing changes made since. TabState.copyFromCache
is where every saved state is read from the tab's cache, and
_restoreTabEntry is where saved fields are handed to the page, so data
already in a profile is never put back either. No chrome API decides
which pages' fields the session store keeps. SvalPreferences decides
which form data is Settings'.

